# What the four tests pin, from rust-quepaxa 0.1.0 `RecorderCore::inform_decision`:
#   * slot <= pruned_through            -> Ok(()), no state recreated;
#   * same slot, same value_ids         -> Ok(()), the recorded decision stands;
#   * same slot, different value_ids    -> Err(ConflictingDecision { slot });
#   * any other slot                    -> recorded.
# `DurableRecorderCore::inform_decisions` applies a batch through one `mutate`:
# a refusal restores the pre-batch snapshot before returning, and the store save
# happens only after the whole batch succeeded, so a refused batch is not
# partially durable.

